---
import Eyebrow from './Eyebrow.astro';

const signals = [
  {
    title: 'Every deploy goes straight to prod.',
    desc: 'There’s no staging environment, so the first place new code meets real users is production.',
  },
  {
    title: 'main is the only branch that matters.',
    desc: 'Nothing stops a direct push, and nothing reviews a change before it ships.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The test suite is you, clicking around.',
    desc: 'No unit tests, no integration tests, and nothing verifying one tenant can’t read another tenant’s data.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Releases live in your head.',
    desc: 'What’s safe to ship, in what order, and what to do when it breaks — none of it is written down.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Rollback is a theory.',
    desc: 'You’ve never actually rehearsed recovering from a bad deploy, so the first drill will be a real incident.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Schema changes are hand-run.',
    desc: 'The database and the code drift apart because migrations aren’t versioned or synced with deploys.',
  },
];
---

<section id="problem" class="border-t border-border">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-24 md:py-32">
    <Eyebrow text="01 — Where you probably are" />
    <h2 class="mt-6 font-display text-3xl [font-weight:500] md:text-4xl">
      Your product is real. Your release process is you.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-[68ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Shipping straight to prod was the correct tradeoff — it's how you got here. But somewhere
      along the way the product started carrying revenue, and the process didn't change. If most of
      these sound familiar, you're exactly who we built this for:
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-12 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
      {
        signals.map(({ title, desc }) => (
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <span class="mt-2 h-2 w-2 shrink-0 bg-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold">{title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-1 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">{desc}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-12 max-w-[68ch] text-lg leading-relaxed">
      None of this means you built it wrong. It means the product outgrew the process — and the fix
      is installation, not a rewrite.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
